Authors: @joshspicer


[Create Issue](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/new?template=blank&body=Testing+%23329614%0A%0A&assignees=joshspicer)

---

Test the following managed customization settings:

- [`strictPluginOnlyCustomization`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-internalbacklog/issues/8464) — When `true`, standalone user/workspace agents, skills, instructions, hooks, and MCP collections are blocked. Eligible plugin-provided customizations remain available.
- [`allowManagedHooksOnly`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-internalbacklog/issues/8464) — When `true`, standalone hooks are blocked. Plugin hooks run only when their plugin is explicitly enabled through managed `enabledPlugins`; user enablement alone is insufficient.
- [`allowManagedMcpServersOnly`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-internalbacklog/issues/8464) — When `true`, only MCP servers matching managed `allowedMcpServers` are available. `deniedMcpServers` remains restrictive and wins over an overlapping allow.
- [`extraKnownMarketplaces.<name>.autoUpdate`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-internalbacklog/issues/8462) — Controls automatic updates per marketplace. Managed `true` or `false` overrides `extensions.autoUpdate`; an omitted value inherits it. Equivalent GitHub shorthand and URL references receive the same policy.

## Setup

- Use a disposable profile and workspace.
- Install the file using [Test: File-based managed settings](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/323147):
  - macOS: `/Library/Application Support/GitHubCopilot/managed-settings.json`
  - Linux: `/etc/github-copilot/managed-settings.json`
  - Windows: `%ProgramFiles%\GitHubCopilot\managed-settings.json`
- Enable `chat.useHooks`.
- Install `goal` from `microsoft/vscode-team-kit`.
- Install `awesome-copilot` from `github/awesome-copilot#marketplace`.

## Goal

Your goal is to exercise all of these managed settings.  See the links above for how they should behave.  Please feel free to follow your own testing path, as long as you exercise all keys,

### A possible testing path
- Create standalone workspace agent, skill, instruction, hook, and MCP entries.
- Apply the configuration below and run **Developer: Policy Diagnostics**. Confirm each key has source **File (managed-settings.json)**.
- Confirm standalone customizations disappear while the plugin customizations remain.
- Confirm only the managed-enabled `goal` plugin hook can run.
- Confirm `tpi-managed-allowed` is available, `tpi-user-only` is blocked, and `tpi-denied` is blocked despite also being allowed.
- Change the policy file while VS Code is running and confirm discovery updates without a restart.
- For deterministic update testing, replace the marketplace repositories below with test forks containing an older installed plugin and a newer published version.
- With `extensions.autoUpdate` disabled, confirm only the `autoUpdate: true` marketplace updates.
- With `extensions.autoUpdate` enabled, confirm the `autoUpdate: false` marketplace does not update.
- Remove an `autoUpdate` property and confirm that marketplace inherits `extensions.autoUpdate`.
- Configure the same GitHub marketplace using its full URL and confirm it receives the shorthand marketplace’s policy without appearing twice.
- Remove a marketplace from `strictKnownMarketplaces` and confirm automatic, direct, and forced updates from it are blocked.

### Workspace Files

#### `.vscode/mcp/json`

```json

{
  "servers": {
    "tpi-managed-allowed": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["-e", "process.stdin.resume()"]
    },
    "tpi-user-only": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["-e", "process.stdin.resume()"]
    },
    "tpi-denied": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["-e", "process.stdin.resume()"]
    }
  },
  "inputs": []
}
```



#### Example `managed-settings.json` (see install location above)

```json
{
  "strictPluginOnlyCustomization": true,
  "allowManagedHooksOnly": true,
  "allowManagedMcpServersOnly": true,
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "goal@vscode-team-kit": true,
    "awesome-copilot@awesome-copilot": true
  },
  "allowedMcpServers": [
    {
      "serverName": "awesome-copilot"
    },
    {
      "serverName": "tpi-managed-allowed"
    },
    {
      "serverName": "tpi-denied"
    }
  ],
  "deniedMcpServers": [
    {
      "serverName": "tpi-denied"
    }
  ],
  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "vscode-team-kit": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "microsoft/vscode-team-kit"
      },
      "autoUpdate": true
    },
    "awesome-copilot": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "github/awesome-copilot",
        "ref": "marketplace"
      },
      "autoUpdate": false
    }
  },
  "strictKnownMarketplaces": [
    {
      "source": "github",
      "repo": "microsoft/vscode-team-kit"
    },
    {
      "source": "github",
      "repo": "github/awesome-copilot",
      "ref": "marketplace"
    }
  ]
}
```
